  "id": "Compound::DB01127 - Gene::1588",
  "verbalization": "Econazole, a broad-spectrum antifungal agent, is linked to Cyp19a1 through a series of structural and functional relationships. The evidence suggests that Econazole, which resembles Isoconazole and Sertaconazole, shares a common ancestor with Tioconazole, which in turn binds to Cyp19a1. This implies that the antifungal activity of Econazole may be mediated through a similar mechanism as its structural relatives, potentially involving the cytochrome P450 enzyme Cyp19a1. The recurring evidence of binding to Cyp19a1 across multiple pathways highlights a possible role in drug metabolism or interaction. The integration of these pathways supports the hypothesis that Econazole's antifungal effects may be linked to its interaction with Cyp19a1, though the exact mechanism of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
